course: dictionary
lesson: 13709
title: Inspired: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer wants. Inspired is one of these words. «I felt inspired to paint a huge picture of the sea.» Here inspired means filled with a strong wish to create something.
explain: «The book inspired me to start writing stories.» Here inspired is the past of inspire, which means to give someone new ideas or courage. Ask yourself: who or what did the inspiring? The book did, so the word is working as a verb.
explain: «The bridge was an inspired design.» Here inspired means very clever or good. Try swapping in clever or good: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning. Then check the words around it for clues.
explain: «A film inspired by a true story» means a film based on, or caused by, a true story. Look for the words inspired by. When you see them together, the meaning is usually based on or caused by.
fact: Inspired can mean filled with a strong wish to do something good or creative.
fact: Inspired is also the past form of inspire, which means to give someone new ideas or courage.
fact: «An inspired idea» means a very clever or good idea.
fact: «Inspired by» means based on or caused by, as in «a song inspired by the rain».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The team felt inspired after the coach's speech, so they played their best game.» What does inspired mean here? | Bored of the game | Angry with the referee | *Filled with a strong wish to do well | Tired and sleepy
exercise: «Her teacher's story inspired Maya to become a scientist.» What does inspired mean here? | *Gave Maya new ideas and courage | Lost | Painted | Forgot
exercise: «The film was inspired by a true story about a brave dog.» What does inspired by mean here? | *Based on a true story | Read aloud in class | Shorter than a true story | Spoiled by a true story
test: «Grandma's plan to fix the old boat was an inspired idea.» What does an inspired idea mean? | Silly and messy | *A very clever or good idea | An idea copied from a book | An idea that nobody likes
test: «I felt inspired to write a poem about the stars.» Which word tells you the poem was an active choice? | *Felt | Stars | Write | Poem
exam: «The artist said the storm inspired her best painture, and everyone wanted to see it.» What does inspired most likely mean here? | Wrapped up | *Caused, or gave her the idea for | Frightened | Cancelled
